    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "616ddeab86082ca06f339094f577609f",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1983,
    "chunk_text": "Govt. accepts responsibility for students with disabilities: PM\n\nBuilding a respectful education system that treats everyone equally is a fundamental objective of the Government, while it has also accepted the responsibility of ensuring a better future for students with disabilities, Prime Minister Dr. Harini Amarasuriya said.\n\nThe Prime Minister made these remarks while participating in the \u201cSarasavi Dirio Abhiman\u201d ceremony organised by the President\u2019s Fund to recognise university students with disabilities at the Swami Vipulananda Institute of Aesthetic Studies of the Eastern University yesterday (12).\n\nAs part of the third phase of the programme, the Prime Minister presented certificates of appreciation and financial assistance of Rs.100,000 each to 50 students with disabilities studying at the Eastern and South-Eastern universities in the Eastern Province.\n\nThe Prime Minister also appreciated the support extended by the Eastern Provincial Divisional Secretariats and Divisional Secretaries in implementing the activities of the President\u2019s Fund at the regional level.\n\nAddressing the gathering, Dr. Amarasuriya said she was proud of the students who had overcome numerous challenges without giving up and continued their education.\n\n\u201cI feel very proud of all of you. You have set a good example to the world about how to move forward without giving up despite the challenges,\u201d she said.\n\nShe also expressed her gratitude to the parents of the students for protecting, supporting and caring for them throughout their journey.\n\nThe Prime Minister said that, in line with the Government\u2019s policy vision of \u201cA rich country is a beautiful life,\u201d the Government was working to build a respectful society through an education system that treats everyone equally.\n\nShe said the Government had already taken steps to provide a monthly allowance of Rs.5,000 to university students from low-income families as well as schoolchildren from low-income families."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-09-12-dailymirrorlk-9a08c607",
    "num": "dailymirrorlk-9a08c607",
    "date_str": "2026-09-12",
    "description": "Govt. accepts responsibility for students with disabilities: PM",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.dailymirror.lk/breaking-news/Govt-accepts-responsibility-for-students-with-disabilities-PM/108-350162",
