    "md5": "1ad68a751d46ee559c1ca190b8ee6f63",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 980,
    "chunk_text": "One dead, 102 rescued from Indonesian ferry that went missing in Java Sea\n\nBBC - One person has died and 102 have been rescued from a stricken Indonesian passenger ferry in the Java Sea, an official said.\n\nA search and rescue operation was launched after contact was lost with the Virgo Transport 8 ship, which was carrying 243 people, as it encountered bad weather, Indonesia's search and rescue agency said.\n\nThe ferry was travelling from Surabaya to the south Kalimantan city of Banjarmasin and was last reported to be about 150km south of Banjarmasin around 02:00 local time on Sunday.\n\nSearch and rescue ships and a helicopter have been deployed to the scene and all other vessels in that area of the Java Sea have been alerted to report signs of any passengers.\n\nThe incident comes after a separate ferry in Indonesia caught fire off Madura island last month, killing five.\n\nThe Indonesian archipelago has more than 17,000 islands and ferries are a common form of transport."
