    "chunk_text": "Businessman arrested at BIA with Rs. 6.68 mn worth of \u2018Kush\u2019\n\nColombo, Sep. 13 (Daily Mirror) - A 44-year-old businessman from Weligama, Matara, was arrested yesterday by Customs officers at the Bandaranaike International Airport (BIA) after he was allegedly found attempting to smuggle 668 grams of \u2018Kush\u2019 valued at around Rs. 6.68 million into the country.\n\nThe suspect had arrived at the BIA from Bangkok, Thailand, on SriLankan Airlines flight UL-405 at around 4.30 p.m. on September 12, Customs officials said.\n\nAccording to Customs, the suspect had attempted to pass through the Red Channel while carrying the consignment concealed in the two side pockets of the jacket he was wearing.\n\nThe 668-gram stock of \u2018Kush\u2019 had been packed into three pellets and tightly wrapped with sellotape, officials said.\n\nThe suspect and the seized drugs were subsequently handed over to officers of the Katunayake Airport Police Narcotics Bureau for further investigations."
