    "chunk_text": "\u201cWhile the drought is a natural challenge, the suffering caused by human cruelty is preventable. Shooting animals, setting up illegal electric fences or laying poison can turn an already difficult situation into a tragedy,\u201d the Ministry said.\n\nThe Ministry urged the public, particularly communities living close to wildlife habitats, to refrain from harming animals and instead allow them to move safely in search of water and food.\n\n\u201cFar harsher than the drought in nature is the drought of empathy in human hearts. The true denizens of the wild also have a rightful place on this Earth,\u201d the Ministry said.\n\nThe Ministry called on the public to support efforts to protect wildlife during the dry spell, stressing that safeguarding animals was not merely a conservation responsibility but also a reflection of the country\u2019s compassion and respect for life."
